cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use copul in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "copul: copulas and dependence measures in Python"
abstract: >-
  copul is a Python package for research on copulas and dependence measures.
  It combines symbolic copula families (SymPy) with a vectorised numerical
  API, a numerical engine for rank correlations and measures of dependence
  such as Chatterjee's xi, exact formulas for checkerboard, Bernstein and
  shuffle-of-min copulas, statistical estimation and fitting, and research
  tools for exact regions between measures, optimisation over checkerboard
  copulas and counterexample search.
type: software
authors:
